{
  "what_this_is": [
    "PERCEPTUAL-ORGANS-002 Lane A. Hand-authored Perception Lab records, validated by BOTH",
    "runtimes: `backend/tests/test_perception_lab_contracts.py` loads each one through the Pydantic",
    "model named here, and `frontend/src/perceptionLab/contract/perceptionLab.parity.test.js` loads",
    "the same file through the JavaScript validator and checks that every declared",
    "`frontend_consumed_fields` path resolves.",
    "They are the examples Lanes B-E build against. A lane whose output does not validate here has",
    "not implemented this contract."
  ],
  "coverage": {
    "run_outcomes": "all six — ready, empty, unavailable, refused, partial, failed",
    "execution_identities": "all three — LIVE, REPLAY, FIXTURE",
    "payload_variants": "all four — extent_set, topology_relation_set, negative_space_field, refusal",
    "planner_identities": "all three — direct, rules (as a declared fallback from model), model",
    "session_modes": "both — isolation and chain",
    "review_verdicts": "correct and wrong, with corrections on the second"
  },
  "form_payloads": {
    "what_this_is": [
      "PERCEPTUAL-FORMS-001A. One committed payload per registered perceptual form, under",
      "`forms/`, validated by BOTH runtimes against the model the form registry names.",
      "THESE ARE PAYLOADS, NOT ARTIFACTS, and the distinction is load-bearing. Sixteen of the",
      "nineteen forms have an empty `produced_by_operations`, so no artifact of them can exist",
      "yet — an artifact names the operation that produced it. A full artifact fixture for those",
      "sixteen would have to name an operation that never ran, and a fixture that lies about its",
      "provenance is worse than no fixture. The payload alone claims nothing about who made it,",
      "and it is the part the next lane must not reinvent."
    ],
